# Line-ending policy for the whole repository.
#
# Without this file the behaviour depends on each machine's core.autocrlf,
# which on this project is set by the Git for Windows installer at SYSTEM
# scope — invisible to the repository and not shared with anyone else. Two
# developers can therefore check out different bytes from the same commit.
#
# The repository stores LF for every text file. It already did before this
# file existed; this makes that a rule rather than an accident.

# Detect text automatically, and check it out with LF on every platform.
# Every consumer of this repository that cares about line endings is Linux:
# the containers, the CI runner, and the VPS. Windows editors handle LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed inside Linux containers — CRLF here is not a cosmetic problem, it
# breaks the shebang and the psql heredocs. Restated explicitly so the rule
# survives anyone narrowing the wildcard above.
*.sh               text eol=lf
.husky/*           text eol=lf

# Read by the nginx container's envsubst entrypoint at start-up.
*.template         text eol=lf
*.template.example text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text. Git already detects these by
# content; stating it removes the guesswork.
*.xlsx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
